@startuml
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Segoe UI
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam ArrowColor #0b7a75
skinparam ComponentBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam DatabaseBorderColor #6b7280
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #f3f4f6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #9ca3af
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #0b7a75
skinparam SequenceLifeLineBorderColor #9ca3af

title A person opens a provider detail: click to paint, no model on the path

actor "Person" as P
participant "ProviderDetailWidget\n(React, in the iframe)" as W
participant "ClientRouter\n(wrapper)" as CR
participant "Gate\n(facade)" as GATE
participant "UniversalNavigator\n(SharedServices)" as UN
database "sessions + render ledger\n(repo rows)" as REPO
participant "UniversalNavigatorProxy\n(FindCare)" as PXY
participant "provider_detail tool\n(FindCare)" as PDT

P -> W : clicks the detail link on a provider card
W -> CR : postMessage router:makeCall\naction 'provider_detail', payload {npi}
CR -> GATE : POST  (route: client_sessioned)\nsession_token + head + params\nAccept: application/x-ndjson

note right of GATE
  The gate knows only transport. It
  collects the token, head and params
  and hands them on. It has no routes
  and decides nothing.
end note

GATE -> UN : pass(token, head, params)

UN -> REPO : load session by GUID
UN -> UN : verify + restamp nonce\n(session-security helpers)
note right of UN
  Session security lives in the navigator
  now, not in app.py. The gate never
  validates.
end note

UN -> UN : route from the map (registry);\nparameters vs state -- a conflict raises
UN -> UN : subscription dispatch:\nroute -> provider_detail

UN -> REPO : ledger: record the expectation
note left of REPO
  Dispatch records the expectation; the
  completion callback closes it; timeout
  facts race the callback. If the page is
  not rendered in time, the navigator
  responds.
end note

UN -> PXY : dispatch across the wire\n(tool_to_tool)
PXY -> PDT : relay locally (function call)
PDT -> PDT : build the detail\n(recursion-guarded)
PDT --> PXY : detail document
PXY --> UN : internal_callback\n(proof: our_signature)

UN -> REPO : ledger: close the entry;\nmerge serially (shared lib)
UN -> GATE : stream the event\n(the gate owns the one stream)
GATE -> CR : event: provider_detail
CR -> W : router:event-broadcast
W -> W : renders the panel it claimed

UN -> REPO : persist the mutated user_object
UN -> GATE : final {ok, guid,\ntime_remaining_seconds, session_token}
GATE -> CR : router:final
CR -> W : turn complete

note over P, PDT #f3f4f6
  No language model runs anywhere on this path. The person named the
  record by working a control, so there is nothing to interpret: the
  gesture is dispatched by subscription, one tool answers through its
  proxy, and the gate writes the one stream. The UtteranceManager is
  not reached.
end note

@enduml
